# Object Model v4 Tags
@protocol-accelerating-delivery @protocol-validation @protocol-metrics
@journey-cross-functional @phase-align-outcomes @measurement-framework

Feature: Accelerating Delivery Protocol Validation and Metrics
  As a manager or squad member
  I want to validate protocol execution and track success metrics
  So that we ensure the protocol delivers measurable value and maintains team alignment

  Background:
    Given the accelerating delivery protocol is being executed by a cross-functional squad
    And outcome alignment, JTBD identification, and work reorganization phases are in progress
    And measurement frameworks and tracking mechanisms are established
    And stakeholders require visibility into protocol effectiveness

  @protocol-checklist @validation-framework
  Scenario: Execute comprehensive protocol validation checklist
    Given the protocol execution is complete or in progress
    When the validation checklist is applied
    Then every task/action is explicitly mapped to a measurable user or customer outcome
    And only top Opportunity Score JTBDs are in focus with lower-value items parked
    And success metrics are defined, tracked, and visible for leadership and team
    And all backlog/work outputs trace directly to outcome with unmapped items paused/stopped
    And BDD, Issue, and Outcome mappings are complete and up to date
    And "Did we actually deliver value?" validation is greenlit by all team members

  @manager-metrics @quick-dashboard
  Scenario: Track quick metrics for busy managers
    Given managers need rapid visibility into protocol effectiveness
    When manager metrics dashboard is reviewed
    Then percentage of team work aligned to outcome shows greater than 90%
    And cycle time to outcome alignment is less than 5 days from kickoff
    And team clarity/alignment score via NPS self-report is greater than 8/10
    And reduction in waste shows percentage of effort NOT tied to agreed outcome approaching zero
    And measurable business/customer impact shows direct metric results linked to shipped work

  @weekly-tracking @continuous-monitoring
  Scenario: Maintain weekly tracking cadence for protocol metrics
    Given the protocol is in active execution
    When weekly metric collection occurs
    Then cycle time to full outcome clarity is measured and trended
    And percent of all work mapped directly to defined outcome is calculated (target >90%)
    And user adoption statistics are gathered and analyzed
    And team self-assessment scores for clarity and alignment are collected
    And business impact metrics are updated with latest measurement data
    And any drift from target metrics triggers immediate corrective action

  @business-impact-validation @outcome-measurement
  Scenario: Validate measurable business and customer impact
    Given the squad has been executing work aligned to their defined outcome
    When business and customer impact is measured
    Then direct metric results demonstrate progress toward outcome achievement
    And customer/user behavior shows measurable improvement in targeted areas
    And business metrics (revenue, activation, satisfaction) show positive correlation
    And the link between shipped work and metric improvement is clearly established
    And impact measurement validates that the protocol delivers on its value proposition

  @real-world-metrics @sales-dashboard-success
  Scenario: Track sales dashboard protocol success metrics
    Given the sales dashboard squad is executing the protocol for pipeline insights outcome
    When success metrics are tracked weekly
    Then adoption statistics show how many sales users have switched from manual methods
    And user interaction analytics demonstrate sub-30-second response times for top questions
    And sales leader satisfaction scores indicate improved pipeline visibility
    And feature usage data validates alignment with the 95% adoption goal
    And engineering velocity metrics show reduced context-switching and rework

  @early-warning-system @drift-detection
  Scenario: Detect and respond to protocol drift early
    Given the protocol is in execution with established metrics
    When metrics indicate potential drift from protocol discipline
    Then work alignment percentage dropping below 90% triggers immediate review
    And team clarity scores declining below 8/10 prompt alignment sessions
    And cycle time extending beyond 5 days initiates process improvement
    And increasing waste percentage signals need for ruthless prioritization refresh
    And stakeholder satisfaction declining indicates communication gaps requiring attention

  @retrospective-analysis @continuous-improvement
  Scenario: Conduct protocol retrospective for continuous improvement
    Given a protocol execution cycle has completed
    When the squad conducts a retrospective analysis
    Then what worked well in maintaining outcome focus is identified
    And obstacles to alignment and delivery are documented
    And metric trends are analyzed for improvement opportunities
    And stakeholder feedback is collected and synthesized
    And process refinements are identified for future protocol executions
    And lessons learned are documented for organizational knowledge sharing

  @cross-reference-integrity @object-model-compliance
  Scenario: Maintain Object Model v4 cross-reference integrity
    Given the protocol involves multiple business objects and cross-references
    When cross-reference integrity is validated
    Then JTBD-to-Outcome mappings are complete and current
    And Outcome-to-Work Item traceability is maintained
    And BDD-to-Protocol Task relationships are documented
    And Issue-to-Outcome links are preserved and updated
    And all Object Model v4 tags and identifiers are properly maintained
    And cross-reference arrays are populated with accurate related entity IDs
